{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ובקשתם", :translit "u-vikashtem", :gloss "and you seek"} {:he "ובקשתם גם כהונה", :translit "u-vikashtem gam kehunah", :gloss "and you seek also the priesthood"} {:he "ובקשתם משם את ה' אלהיך", :translit "u-vikashtem misham et Hashem Elokeikha", :gloss "and you seek from there the LORD your God"} {:he "ובקשתם אותי וגו'", :translit "u-vikashtem oti ve-gomer", :gloss "and you seek Me etc."} {:he "בירמיה על הגלות", :translit "bi-Yirmeyahu al ha-galut", :gloss "in Jeremiah concerning the exile"} {:he "כשתבקשו אותי בגלות בתשובה ותגאלו אז", :translit "keshe-tevakshu oti ba-galut bi-teshuvah ve-tiga'elu az", :gloss "when you seek Me in exile through repentance you will then be redeemed"} {:he "ובקשתם גם כהונה שהיא בטלה מכם כל זמן שאתם בגלות", :translit "u-vikashtem gam kehunah she-hi batelah mikhem kol zman she-atem ba-galut", :gloss "and you seek also the priesthood which is annulled from you all the time you are in exile"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ובקשתם גם כהונה" "ובקשתם משם את ה' אלהיך" "ובקשתם אותי"]} {:kind :other, :note "Geza equal root links verse about seeking priesthood to verses about seeking God in exile"}], :frame {:text "The Masorah records three occurrences of the identical phrase 'and you seek' (u-vikashtem): at Numbers 16:10 (Korah seeking priesthood), at Deuteronomy 4:29 ('and you seek from there the LORD your God'), and at Jeremiah 29:13 ('and you seek Me'). Deuteronomy 4:29 addresses Israel in exile: 'from there you will seek the LORD your God, and you will find Him.' Jeremiah 29:13 is addressed to the Babylonian exiles: 'You will seek Me and find Me when you search with all your heart.' The priesthood's cessation in exile is addressed at Hosea 3:4, which states Israel will be many days 'without ephod,' a priestly vestment.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 4:29" "Jeremiah 29:13" "Hosea 3:4"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ובקשתם גם כהונה" "ובקשתם משם